  "d2784e3c8e7297f5aaaa5fc70d1d286494a3e47c5edeb73eaa6dd4f3348fb7cd": {
    "fact_rationales": {
      "F11": "Ground-glass trabecular pattern is seen in both fibrous dysplasia and juvenile ossifying fibroma, but the presence of radiolucency around the roots of deciduous teeth and erupting premolars is more characteristic of juvenile ossifying fibroma.",
      "F13": "Expansion of the buccal and palatal cortical plates and involvement of more than half of the right maxillary sinus are features that can be seen in both fibrous dysplasia and juvenile ossifying fibroma, but are more commonly associated with juvenile ossifying fibroma.",
      "F14": "A well-defined margin is more characteristic of juvenile ossifying fibroma, whereas fibrous dysplasia typically has a poorly defined margin.",
      "F16": "The well-defined margin of the lesion is more consistent with juvenile ossifying fibroma, making fibrous dysplasia less likely."
    },
